ook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>BABCOCK-HITACHI KABUSHIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJISAWA, MASATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, YASUYOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAMOTO, EIJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA, KOUICHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJISAWA MASATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATO YASUYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYAMOTO EIJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA KOUICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJISAWA, MASATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATO, YASUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAMOTO, EIJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOKOYAMA, KOUICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p> An exhaust emission control catalyst structure which is disposed in an exhaust gas flow path and facilitates an exhaust emission control, wherein platy catalysts (1) and gas dispersing bodies comprising metal, ceramic or glass netty substances (7) having many holes passing therethrough or linear, band-shaped or rod-shaped materials are alternately laminated to disturb an exhaust gas flow through the gas flow path so as to improve contact between the untreated gas and the catalysts, thereby making the structure suitable for a high-efficient, compact exhaust emission control system.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne une structure catalytique permettant de réguler les émissions d'échappement, laquelle structure est disposée dans la voie d'écoulement des gaz d'échappement et permet de faciliter la régulation des émissions d'échappement. Des catalyseurs lamellaires (1) et des corps de dispersion des gaz comprenant des substances métallique, céramique ou de verre réticulée (7) traversées de nombreux trous, ou des matériaux linéaires, en forme de bande ou en forme de tige sont stratifiés par alternance de manière à perturber le flux de gaz d'échappement dans la voie d'écoulement des gaz, et à améliorer ainsi le contact entre les gaz non traités et les catalyseurs. On obtient ainsi une structure adaptée pour un système de régulation des émissions d'échappement compact et d'une grande efficacité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>